    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "Watch the three assigned videos and add "
        },
        {
          "text": "two annotations to each",
          "bold": true
        },
        {
          "text": ", for a total of "
        },
        {
          "text": "six annotations",
          "bold": true
        },
        {
          "text": ". Anchor every annotation to a precise moment and select the tag that best identifies what you are analyzing. In "
        },
        {
          "text": "2–4 sentences (50–75 words)",
          "bold": true
        },
        {
          "text": ", describe the specific detail you notice and explain how it shapes memory, testimony, inheritance, or historical experience. Focus on close analysis rather than summarizing the whole work."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "children": [
        {
          "text": ""
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "The tag identifies the "
        },
        {
          "text": "musical, verbal, or visual element",
          "bold": true
        },
        {
          "text": " under discussion; your annotation explains what that element is doing and why it matters."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "children": [
        {
          "text": ""
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "children": [
        {
          "text": ""
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "heading-three",
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "Tags",
          "underline": true,
          "bold": true
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "heading-three",
      "children": [
        {
          "underline": true,
          "bold": true,
          "text": ""
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "Sound",
          "bold": true
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "bulleted-list",
      "children": [
        {
          "type": "list-item",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "Vocals",
              "bold": true
            },
            {
              "text": " — singing, rap delivery, vocal tone, breath, phrasing, or emphasis"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "list-item",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "Rhythm",
              "bold": true
            },
            {
              "text": " — pulse, groove, flow, pacing, syncopation, or rhythmic change"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "list-item",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "Instrumentation",
              "bold": true
            },
            {
              "text": " — instruments, electronic sounds, ensemble roles, or distinctive timbres"
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "",
          "bold": true
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "children": [
        {
          "bold": true,
          "text": "Form"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "bulleted-list",
      "children": [
        {
          "type": "list-item",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "Structure",
              "bold": true
            },
            {
              "text": " — sections, repetition, transitions, buildup, return, or overall organization"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "list-item",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "Texture",
              "bold": true
            },
            {
              "text": " — layering, density, sparseness, and interaction among voices or sounds"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "list-item",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "Dynamics",
              "bold": true
            },
            {
              "text": " — changes in volume, intensity, restraint, force, or climax"
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "",
          "bold": true
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "children": [
        {
          "bold": true,
          "text": "Words"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "bulleted-list",
      "children": [
        {
          "type": "list-item",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "Lyrics",
              "bold": true
            },
            {
              "text": " — sung or rapped words, verbal imagery, storytelling, or recurring lines"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "list-item",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "Speech",
              "bold": true
            },
            {
              "text": " — testimony, narration, dialogue, interviews, or other spoken voices"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "list-item",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "Language",
              "bold": true
            },
            {
              "text": " — accent, diction, code-switching, translation, or movement among languages"
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "",
          "bold": true
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "children": [
        {
          "bold": true,
          "text": "Image"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "bulleted-list",
      "children": [
        {
          "type": "list-item",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "Movement",
              "bold": true
            },
            {
              "text": " — gesture, choreography, posture, facial expression, or bodily action"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "list-item",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "Staging",
              "bold": true
            },
            {
              "text": " — setting, lighting, costume, props, and arrangement of people or objects in space"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "list-item",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "Framing",
              "bold": true
            },
            {
              "text": " — camera angle, shot distance, composition, perspective, and what the image includes or excludes"
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "children": [
        {
          "text": ""
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "An effective annotation identifies something concrete, interprets its significance, and remains closely tied to the selected moment."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "children": [
        {
          "text": ""
        }
      ]
    }
